        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "2. Experimental procedures",
          "quote": "Alloys were prepared from high purity (>99.9%) elements by vacuum arc melting in a water-cooled Cu hearth. A low pressure high-purity argon atmosphere additionally purified with a Ti getter was used to produce the arc. To ensure complete dissolution and mixing of the alloying elements in liquid state, each sample was flipped-over and re-melted at least five times. The weight of each sample was 200 g and the sample dimensions were approximately 100 mm × 30 mm x 12 mm, with rounded surfaces.",
